ft_swap
Turn-in directory: ex02/
Files to turn in: ft_swap.c
Allowed functions: None
• Create a function that swaps the values of two integers using their addresses received
as parameters.
• The function should be prototyped as follows:
void ft_swap(int *a, int *b);

*******

My idea was:
void ft_swap(int *a, int *b)
{
 *a = A
 *b = B
 *a = B
 *b = A
}

Wrong.
the system doesn't know A and B, and there is not temporal variable to restore the values.
So we may need a temporal variable named temp, then:
int temp;
temp = *a;
*a = *b;
*b = temp

void ft_swap(int *a, int *b)
{
 int temp;

 temp = *a;
 *a = *b;
 *b = temp
}

If I want to test it well, I can create the main() inside a comment and then test it removing the /* and */ easily.
#include <stdio.h>

void ft_swap(int *a, int *b);

#include <stdio.h>

int     main(void)
{
        int     a;
        int     b;

        a = 3;
        b = 5;
        printf("before: a=%d, b=%d\n", a, b);
        ft_swap(&a, &b);
        printf("after: a=%d, b=%d\n", a, b);
